6.11 Helios shall maintain proper books of account and records relating to the Services and shall, upon reasonable notice, make such records available for inspection by the Client or its appointed auditors during normal business hours for the purpose of verifying the accuracy of any invoice or statement rendered under this Article 6.

**7. CLIENT OBLIGATIONS**

7.1 The Client shall provide Helios with safe and unhindered access to the Facilities at all reasonable times for the purpose of performing the Services, and shall ensure that Helios personnel are not obstructed or delayed in the performance of their duties.

7.2 The Client shall provide Helios, at no cost to Helios, with:
(a) access to water and electricity supplies at each Facility;
(b) a secure area for the storage of Helios's tools, equipment, and spare parts;
(c) suitable office accommodation and communication facilities at each Facility; and
(d) such information, documentation, and data as Helios may reasonably require to perform the Services, including but not limited to as-built drawings, equipment manuals, and operational records.

7.3 The Client shall ensure that the Facilities are operated in accordance with the manufacturer's specifications and with good industry practice, and shall promptly notify Helios of any abnormal operating conditions, faults, or damage to the Facilities of which it becomes aware.

7.4 The Client shall obtain and maintain all permits, licences, and consents required for the operation of the Facilities and for the performance of the Services, other than those which are the responsibility of Helios under Article 8.
**8. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY**

8.1 Subject to Article 8.5, neither Party shall be liable to the other Party for any indirect, special, incidental, or consequential loss or damage, including but not limited to loss of profit, loss of revenue, loss of production, loss of business opportunity, loss of goodwill, or loss of or corruption to data, arising out of or in connection with this Contract, whether arising in contract, tort (including negligence), breach of statutory duty, or otherwise.

8.2 Subject to Article 8.5, the aggregate liability of Helios to the Client in respect of all claims arising out of or in connection with this Contract, whether arising in contract, tort (including negligence), breach of statutory duty, or otherwise, shall not exceed one hundred percent (100%) of the aggregate Fees paid or payable by the Client to Helios during the twelve (12) month period immediately preceding the date on which the cause of action first arose.

8.3 Subject to Article 8.5, the aggregate liability of the Client to Helios in respect of all claims arising out of or in connection with this Contract, whether arising in contract, tort (including negligence), breach of statutory duty, or otherwise, shall not exceed the aggregate Fees paid or payable by the Client to Helios under this Contract.

8.4 Neither Party shall be liable for any delay or failure to perform its obligations under this Contract to the extent that such delay or failure is caused by a Force Majeure Event, as defined in Article 13.

8.5 Nothing in this Article 8 shall operate to exclude or limit either Party's liability for:
(a) death or personal injury caused by its negligence or the negligence of its personnel, agents, or subcontractors;
(b) fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation;
(c) wilful misconduct or gross negligence;
(d) breach of Article 15 (Confidentiality);
(e) breach of Article 17 (Compliance with Laws and Anti-Bribery); or
(f) any other liability which cannot be excluded or limited by applicable law.

8.6 The Client acknowledges that the Fees have been calculated in reliance upon the limitations and exclusions of liability set out in this Article 8, and that such limitations and exclusions are fair and reasonable in all the circumstances, having regard to the nature of the Services, the availability of insurance, and the scope of the Services to be performed under this Contract.

8.7 Helios shall maintain, at its own cost, appropriate insurance policies with reputable insurers, including:
(a) employer's liability insurance in respect of its personnel;
(b) public liability insurance with a limit of not less than NGN 500,000,000 (Five Hundred Million Naira) per occurrence;
(c) professional indemnity insurance with a limit of not less than NGN 250,000,000 (Two Hundred and Fifty Million Naira) per claim; and
(d) all-risks insurance in respect of Helios's tools, equipment, and spare parts.
Helios shall, upon the Client's reasonable request, provide certificates of insurance or other reasonable evidence of the maintenance of such insurances. Any deductibles or excesses under such policies shall be for the account of Helios.

**9. WARRANTIES**

9.1 Helios warrants that:
(a) it has the full power and authority to enter into and perform its obligations under this Contract;
(b) the Services will be performed with reasonable skill, care, and diligence, in accordance with good industry practice, and in compliance with the requirements of this Contract, including the Service Levels set out in Schedule 2;
(c) the personnel assigned to perform the Services will be suitably qualified, trained, and experienced;
(d) all spare parts and materials supplied by Helios in the performance of the Services will be new, of good quality, and fit for their intended purpose, unless otherwise agreed in writing;
(e) it will comply with all applicable laws, regulations, and codes of practice in the performance of the Services; and
(f) it holds all permits, licences, and consents required for the performance of the Services.

