Description: Proposed change to add drone-based aerial inspections of the solar PV arrays and overhead transmission lines at the Sokoto East site. The inspection programme is intended to supplement the existing ground-based thermal imaging and visual checks, particularly in areas where access is difficult or where vegetation encroachment has been an issue. Scope: conduct two aerial inspection campaigns per year (wet season and dry season), covering all PV modules, string combiner boxes, and the 33 kV overhead line route for a distance of 12 km from the substation. Deliverables include high-resolution imagery, thermal orthomosaics, a defect report with GPS-tagged findings, and a comparison report against the previous campaign.
